  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CommAddDisc 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your advocacy organization has been invited to attend a meeting with
    a research team that is testing several drug compounds that might become part
    of a new cancer treatment. You\u2019ve never attended a meeting like this before,
    so you ask a fellow advocate about it. She explains, \u201CAt this early stage,
    input from community advocates \u2014 like what kinds of cancer treatments would
    be most meaningful to patients \u2014 can help shape research priorities and
    guide which drug compound(s) the team focuses on.\u201D\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: "Even though community advocates aren\u2019t conducting lab experiments,
    their perspective helps researchers understand what matters most to cancer patients.
    This input can guide decisions about which directions are most important to explore
    in the discovery stage. By sharing what patients and families value, community
    advocates help ensure that early research stays focused on meaningful outcomes
    and real-world needs."
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
